./README.md:3:A tiny invented Python money library. It is not a financial product. Inputs are finite Decimal, decimal strings or integers. Amounts use two decimal places with ROUND_HALF_EVEN (ties-to-even). Minor units are integer cents after that rounding. Formatting supports USD, EUR and GBP, places a negative sign before the symbol, and normalizes a rounded negative zero to an unsigned zero.
